      "raw_text": "To determine how many seconds the faster team wins by, we need to calculate the total time for each team to complete the 4x400 meter relay and then find the difference between the two times.\n\n**Step 1: Calculate the total time for the well-rounded team.**\nThe problem states that each of the four members of this team runs their 400-meter leg in precisely 55 seconds.\nSince there are 4 legs in the relay:\n$$ \\text{Total Time}_{\\text{well-rounded}} = 4 \\times 55 \\text{ seconds} $$\n$$ \\text{Total Time}_{\\text{well-rounded}} = 220 \\text{ seconds} $$\n\n**Step 2: Calculate the total time for the less well-rounded team.**\nThe times for this team form an arithmetic sequence where:\n- The first term ($a_1$) is 60 seconds.\n- The common difference ($d$) is -3 seconds (since each subsequent runner is 3 seconds faster).\n- The number of terms ($n$) is 4.\n\nLet's calculate the time for each runner individually:\n1.  **Runner 1:** $60$ seconds.\n2.  **Runner 2:** $60 - 3 = 57$ seconds.\n3.  **Runner 3:** $57 - 3 = 54$ seconds.\n4.  **Runner 4:** $54 - 3 = 51$ seconds.\n\nNow, sum these times to get the total relay time:\n$$ \\text{Total Time}_{\\text{less well-rounded}} = 60 + 57 + 54 + 51 $$\n$$ \\text{Total Time}_{\\text{less well-rounded}} = 222 \\text{ seconds} $$\n\n*Alternative calculation using the arithmetic series sum formula:*\n$$ S_n = \\frac{n}{2} [2a_1 + (n-1)d] $$\n$$ S_4 = \\frac{4}{2} [2(60) + (4-1)(-3)] $$\n$$ S_4 = 2 [120 + 3(-3)] $$\n$$ S_4 = 2 [120 - 9] $$\n$$ S_4 = 2 [111] = ",
      "answer_text": "To determine how many seconds the faster team wins by, we need to calculate the total time for each team to complete the 4x400 meter relay and then find the difference between the two times.\n\n**Step 1: Calculate the total time for the well-rounded team.**\nThe problem states that each of the four members of this team runs their 400-meter leg in precisely 55 seconds.\nSince there are 4 legs in the relay:\n$$ \\text{Total Time}_{\\text{well-rounded}} = 4 \\times 55 \\text{ seconds} $$\n$$ \\text{Total Time}_{\\text{well-rounded}} = 220 \\text{ seconds} $$\n\n**Step 2: Calculate the total time for the less well-rounded team.**\nThe times for this team form an arithmetic sequence where:\n- The first term ($a_1$) is 60 seconds.\n- The common difference ($d$) is -3 seconds (since each subsequent runner is 3 seconds faster).\n- The number of terms ($n$) is 4.\n\nLet's calculate the time for each runner individually:\n1.  **Runner 1:** $60$ seconds.\n2.  **Runner 2:** $60 - 3 = 57$ seconds.\n3.  **Runner 3:** $57 - 3 = 54$ seconds.\n4.  **Runner 4:** $54 - 3 = 51$ seconds.\n\nNow, sum these times to get the total relay time:\n$$ \\text{Total Time}_{\\text{less well-rounded}} = 60 + 57 + 54 + 51 $$\n$$ \\text{Total Time}_{\\text{less well-rounded}} = 222 \\text{ seconds} $$\n\n*Alternative calculation using the arithmetic series sum formula:*\n$$ S_n = \\frac{n}{2} [2a_1 + (n-1)d] $$\n$$ S_4 = \\frac{4}{2} [2(60) + (4-1)(-3)] $$\n$$ S_4 = 2 [120 + 3(-3)] $$\n$$ S_4 = 2 [120 - 9] $$\n$$ S_4 = 2 [111] = ",
